opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Cosmos transaction construction, sign modes, intent and policy"
description: """
TxBody, AuthInfo, SignDoc and TxRaw; SIGN_MODE_DIRECT and
SIGN_MODE_LEGACY_AMINO_JSON; the message allow-list; the fee model; and the
byte-derived intent layer with allow-list policies over it.

SignDoc binds body_bytes and auth_info_bytes as opaque byte strings, and
TxRaw carries those same bytes back out. They are retained, never re-encoded:
protobuf admits encodings that decode alike and re-encode differently, and a
re-encode would change what the node is being asked to do.

The amino JSON writer is hand-written rather than built on a JSON library.
It is a canonical encoder over signed data -- sorted keys, no whitespace,
omitted empty fields -- and keeping it here is what keeps yojson out of the
offline closure."""
